{#
mail/_bounce.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
"This did not arrive", on our own sent mail.

Renders to nothing for almost every message, and when it does render it is the
most important thing on the screen — so unlike the read-receipt line beside it,
this is an alert and not a footnote. The failure it reports is silent by
nature: the mail was accepted, the compose window closed, and the only other
trace is a machine-generated message sitting in the Inbox.

WHAT IS SHOWN, AND WHY EACH PART
  · the recipient, because a mail to five people that failed for one is not an
    undelivered message and must not read as one
  · the MTA's own diagnostic, because "no such address" and "mailbox full" are
    the same status class and completely different problems
  · the status code, quietly, because it is the only unambiguous thing in a
    DSN and someone eventually has to paste it somewhere

NO ACTION BUTTONS. There is no honest one: plMail cannot know whether the
address was a typo, and a "resend" that re-runs the same failure is worse than
nothing. The user reads this and decides.

Variables:
  message  Message
#}
{% if message.bouncedAt is not null %}
    <div role="alert"
         data-testid="bounce-notice"
         class="flex items-start gap-2.5 mt-3 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3">

        <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-xmark text-danger text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>

        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-xs">
            <p class="font-medium text-danger">
                {% if message.bounceRecipient is not empty %}
                    {{ 'message.bounce.failed_for'|trans({'%recipient%': message.bounceRecipient}) }}
                {% else %}
                    {{ 'message.bounce.failed'|trans }}
                {% endif %}
            </p>

            {% if message.bounceDiagnostic is not empty %}
                {# Wrapped and breakable: a diagnostic is frequently one long
                   unbroken token like a URL to a provider's block-list page,
                   and letting it push the column wide breaks the thread. #}
                <p class="mt-1 text-ink-muted break-words">{{ message.bounceDiagnostic }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            <p class="mt-1 text-ink-faint">
                {{ 'message.bounce.reported_at'|trans({
                    '%datetime%': message.bouncedAt|intl_date('dMMM') ~ ', ' ~ message.bouncedAt|date(clock.time),
                }) }}{% if message.bounceStatus is not empty %} · {{ message.bounceStatus }}{% endif %}
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
